After victory, each surrendered foe asks for mercy, after the battle's
closing lines and summary. Answer yes to spare or no to execute.

  yes: the foe leaves without a weapon. No experience or loot.
       Your alignment rises by 5, within the -100 to 100 range.
  no:  the foe is executed. Ordinary kill experience and loot apply,
       using existing damage credit and company sharing.
       Your alignment falls by 5 instead of ordinary kill alignment.

Company alignment is the average of its living members, so its change
may be smaller. Each living companion who witnessed the victory reacts:
those at alignment +25 or above approve mercy; those at -25 or below
approve execution. Approval gives 2 loyalty, disapproval costs 1; others
have no loyalty change. Their beliefs do not change immediately.

The others answer by temperament (help opinions): a devout or cheerful
companion likes mercy, a grim one dislikes it, and so on. A companion that
alignment already moved does not speak twice. Each such answer is 2
loyalty, with the limits that page describes.

You have 30 seconds per displayed question. Invalid answers do not extend
it. With no answer the foe escapes, giving no rewards or alignment change.
Leaving, logout, death, tutorial handoff, restart/copyover, or another battle
releases unanswered foes. Mercy never holds up waiting enemy groups.
If another question is already open, the foes escape instead.
When players share an enemy, only its first battle's owner decides its fate.

The mercy command is used by the question; answer the displayed yes/no prompt.
See also: help morale, help alignment, help combat, help opinions.
